1. She lived in a house share during university with ten other girls. (Verbatim: "we were definitely very good tenants even though we were like 10 girls")
2. She had a roommate who didn’t understand money and frequently delayed paying bills. (Verbatim: "Miss did not understand how money worked. Um, and she was always late paying her bills.")
3. She lived in a house share with a metered electricity system requiring top-ups. (Verbatim: "it had a meter, so we had this card and we had to top it up")
4. She once called the landlord during a weekend to report a gas outage, only to discover he was at his own birthday party. (Verbatim: "he was in the middle of a party and jake and left it to to fix their gas")
5. She remembers the landlord being very kind and adding extra amenities like a fridge and TV. (Verbatim: "he added a lot of more stuff than what we'd even agreed to like he added an extra fridge he added a new television")
6. She cooked meals regularly during her time at university. (Verbatim: "i did cook last night i cook most nights")
7. She made a full English breakfast for a friend, but they declined. (Verbatim: "i was considering making them a full english breakfast but but they didn't want it")
8. She prefers cooking as a way to save money. (Verbatim: "cooking you gotta cook that's how you save money yo")
9. She had a roommate who liked to go jogging at 6–7 a.m. (Verbatim: "they also do a lot of healthy eating i remember i would like be there having my garlic bread while they were toasting kale in the oven")
10. She found it strange that the house was stocked with premium supermarket items like M&S Finest. (Verbatim: "everywhere you looked it was like m and s finest stuff or i don't know what m and s calls it") [end of text]



